IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-weeks`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III.2 Reduction of Premium for Self-Employed Persons Covered by a
-- Plan Established Under a Provincial Law: regs 76.31 to 76.45. Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial
-- plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified against the official text". No section GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATION. Part III.2 repeats Part III.1 for the self-employed person who is covered by a provincial plan: the
-- same disentitlement, reduction of benefits, counting of weeks, and sharing of weeks between two persons caring for the
-- same child, with the Act's sections 152.04, 152.05, 152.14 and 152.21 in place of ss 22, 23, 12 and 67/68. Where the
-- arithmetic is the same arithmetic, the rule here CALLS the rule of Part III.1 (module er4-part3-1-weeks) and cites its
-- own regulation, so that the two Parts cannot disagree about the law; every rule that differs in what it asks is written out.
-- (Weeks and rates as in Part III.1; the Act figures that the formulas read are inputs.)

§ `Regulation 76.31 -- interpretation`

-- src:1324 | 76.31 The following definitions apply in this Part.
-- src:1325 | plan established under a provincial law means a plan, established under a provincial law, that provides for the payment of provincial benefits and in respect of which the premium payable under section 152.21 of the Act is subject to a system for reducing that premium if the payment of allowances, money or other benefits payable under the provincial law would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act. (régime établi en vertu d’une loi provinciale)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.31 "plan established under a provincial law" (src:1324-1325)
GIVEN `the plan is established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premium payable under section 152.21 of the Act is subject to a system for reducing that premium if the payment of allowances, money or other benefits payable under the provincial law would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.31 plan established under a provincial law` IF
        `the plan is established under a provincial law`
    AND `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits`
    AND `the premium payable under section 152.21 of the Act is subject to a system for reducing that premium if the payment of allowances, money or other benefits payable under the provincial law would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`

-- src:1326 | provincial benefits means allowances, money or other benefits, paid to a self-employed person under a plan established under a provincial law because of pregnancy or in respect of the care by that person of one or more of their new-born children or one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption. (prestations provinciales)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.31 "provincial benefits" (src:1326)
GIVEN `the allowances, money or other benefits are paid to a self-employed person under a plan established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid because of pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more of their new-born children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.31 provincial benefits of a self-employed person` IF
        `the allowances, money or other benefits are paid to a self-employed person under a plan established under a provincial law`
    AND (    `they are paid because of pregnancy`
          OR `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more of their new-born children`
          OR `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption`)

§ `Regulation 76.32 -- the standards of a plan established under a provincial law`

-- As in reg 76.03, the Commission's judgments ("substantially the same persons", "substantially equivalent to or greater
-- than") are BOOLEAN inputs (fork F15). There is no "from the day it takes effect" in this regulation.
-- src:1329 | 76.32 A plan established under a provincial law shall meet the following requirements:
-- src:1330 | (a) the plan must provide for the payment of provincial benefits;
-- src:1331 | (b) the plan must, at a minimum, cover substantially the same persons as those who are self-employed persons under the Act;
-- src:1332 | (c) the global amount of provincial benefits payable to a person under the plan must be substantially equivalent to or greater than the global amount of benefits payable to a self-employed person under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act;
-- src:1333 | (d) the plan must provide that an applicant who has received provincial benefits in respect of at least one week under it shall continue to receive such benefits for their full period of entitlement, even if, after receiving provincial benefits in respect of one week, they become a resident of a different province; and
-- src:1334 | (e) the plan must provide for the sharing, by the province with the Government of Canada, of information obtained in the course of administering the plan that is necessary for the administration of a premium reduction system established by this Part, as well as information prepared from that information.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.32 (src:1329-1334)
GIVEN `the plan provides for the payment of provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan covers, at a minimum, substantially the same persons as those who are self-employed persons under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the global amount of provincial benefits payable to a person is substantially equivalent to or greater than the global amount of benefits payable to a self-employed person under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan provides that an applicant who has received provincial benefits in respect of at least one week continues to receive them for the full period of entitlement even after becoming a resident of a different province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan provides for the sharing by the province with the Government of Canada of information obtained in administering the plan that is necessary for the administration of a premium reduction system established by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.32 the plan established under a provincial law meets the requirements` IF
        `the plan provides for the payment of provincial benefits`
    AND `the plan covers, at a minimum, substantially the same persons as those who are self-employed persons under the Act`
    AND `the global amount of provincial benefits payable to a person is substantially equivalent to or greater than the global amount of benefits payable to a self-employed person under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`
    AND `the plan provides that an applicant who has received provincial benefits in respect of at least one week continues to receive them for the full period of entitlement even after becoming a resident of a different province`
    AND `the plan provides for the sharing by the province with the Government of Canada of information obtained in administering the plan that is necessary for the administration of a premium reduction system established by this Part`

§ `Regulations 76.33 to 76.35 -- premium reduction`

-- src:1337 | 76.33 The self-employment premium payable under section 152.21 of the Act shall be reduced as provided by section 76.34 if the payment of provincial benefits would have the effect referred to in subsection 69(2) of the Act in respect of benefits payable to those persons under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.33 (src:1337)
GIVEN `the payment of provincial benefits would have the effect, in respect of benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act, of reducing or eliminating them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.33 the self-employment premium payable under section 152.21 of the Act is to be reduced` IF
    `the payment of provincial benefits would have the effect, in respect of benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act, of reducing or eliminating them`

-- The premium reduction rate is the one reg 76.06 determines. The reduction is that rate applied to the amount the
-- self-employment premium rate is applied to (an input, as in reg 76.05, fork F16).
-- src:1338 | 76.34 The premium reduction to be applied to the self-employment premium shall be calculated by applying the premium reduction rate determined in accordance with section 76.06.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.34 (src:1338)
GIVEN `the amount to which the premium rate is applied` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium reduction rate determined in accordance with section 76.06` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.34 the premium reduction to be applied to the self-employment premium` MEANS
    `the amount to which the premium rate is applied` TIMES `the premium reduction rate determined in accordance with section 76.06`

§ `Regulation 76.36 -- disentitlement`

§§ `Regulation 76.36(2) -- the Commission's determination on the request of the self-employed person`

-- src:1343 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if, at the request of the self-employed person, it is determined by the Commission that the amount of provincial benefits that the self-employed person is entitled to receive is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of benefits that they are entitled to receive under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(2) (src:1343)
GIVEN `the self-employed person has asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has determined that the amount of provincial benefits the self-employed person is entitled to receive is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of benefits they are entitled to receive under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.36(2) subsection (1) does not apply` IF
        `the self-employed person has asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent`
    AND `the Commission has determined that the amount of provincial benefits the self-employed person is entitled to receive is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of benefits they are entitled to receive under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 76.36(1) -- benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05`

-- Whole claim, as in reg 76.09(1) (fork F18).
-- src:1342 | 76.36 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a self-employed person is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act if they are entitled to receive provincial benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(1) (src:1342)
GIVEN `the self-employed person is entitled to receive provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.36(1) the self-employed person is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act` IF
        `the self-employed person is entitled to receive provincial benefits`
    AND (NOT `subsection (2) applies`)

§§ `Regulation 76.36(3) -- any other week of benefits under Part VII.1`

-- src:1344 | (3) Every self-employed person who has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of any week is disentitled to be paid benefits in respect of that same week under Part VII.1 of the Act, other than benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(3) (src:1344)
DECLARE `er4 Benefits claimed by a self-employed person with provincial benefits` IS ONE OF
    `er4 benefits under section 152.04 of the Act`
    `er4 benefits under section 152.05 of the Act`
    `er4 other benefits under Part VII.1 of the Act`
    `er4 benefits of another kind`

-- Benefits under ss 152.04 and 152.05 are excluded from (3) and governed by (1): FALSE; benefits of another kind (for
-- instance under Part I): the subsection says nothing, NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(3) (src:1344)
GIVEN benefits IS A `er4 Benefits claimed by a self-employed person with provincial benefits`
      `the self-employed person has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 76.36(3) the self-employed person is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefits
    WHEN `er4 other benefits under Part VII.1 of the Act` THEN JUST `the self-employed person has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of the week`
    WHEN `er4 benefits of another kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 76.36(4) and (5) -- for greater certainty`

-- src:1345 | (4) For greater certainty, subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of a self-employed person who has applied for and is entitled to receive provincial benefits even if the self-employed person, after making that application, ceases to reside in the province providing those benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(4) (src:1345)
GIVEN `the self-employed person has applied for provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the self-employed person is entitled to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.36(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the self-employed person whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province providing those benefits` IF
        `the self-employed person has applied for provincial benefits`
    AND `the self-employed person is entitled to receive them`

-- src:1346 | (5) For greater certainty, if two persons are caring for the same child or children and one of them is a self-employed person referred to in subsection (4),
-- src:1347 | (a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person if that other person is a self-employed person; and
-- src:1348 | (b) subsections 76.09(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person if that other person is an insured person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(5)(a) (src:1346-1347)
GIVEN `two persons are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them is a self-employed person referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.36(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` IF
        `two persons are caring for the same child or children`
    AND `one of them is a self-employed person referred to in subsection (4)`
    AND `the other person is a self-employed person`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(5)(b) (src:1346, 1348)
GIVEN `two persons are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them is a self-employed person referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.36(5)(b) subsections 76.09(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` IF
        `two persons are caring for the same child or children`
    AND `one of them is a self-employed person referred to in subsection (4)`
    AND `the other person is an insured person`

§ `Regulations 76.37 and 76.38 -- reduction of benefits`

-- src:1351 | 76.37 The benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act to a self-employed person in respect of any week in respect of which the claimant has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits shall be reduced as provided by section 76.38.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.37 (src:1351)
GIVEN `the self-employed person has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.37 the benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act for the week are to be reduced` IF
    `the self-employed person has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits in respect of the week`

-- The same deduction as reg 76.17, "in addition to any deductions referred to in subsections 152.04(4) and 152.05(11)
-- and section 152.18 of the Act" (out of range: piece ei5): the rule calls reg 76.17's.
-- src:1352 | 76.38 An amount equal to the amount of the provincial benefits that a self-employed person has received or is entitled to receive in respect of any week shall be deducted from the amount of benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act to the self-employed person in respect of that same week, in addition to any deductions referred to in subsections 152.04(4) and 152.05(11) and section 152.18 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.38 (src:1352)
GIVEN `the benefits payable for the week after the deductions referred to in subsections 152.04(4) and 152.05(11) and section 152.18 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the provincial benefits the self-employed person has received or is entitled to receive in respect of the same week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.38 the benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` MEANS
    IF `the benefits payable for the week after the deductions referred to in subsections 152.04(4) and 152.05(11) and section 152.18 of the Act` AT LEAST `the provincial benefits the self-employed person has received or is entitled to receive in respect of the same week`
    THEN JUST (`the benefits payable for the week after the deductions referred to in subsections 152.04(4) and 152.05(11) and section 152.18 of the Act` MINUS `the provincial benefits the self-employed person has received or is entitled to receive in respect of the same week`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 76.39 -- no double counting of weeks`

-- src:1355 | 76.39 If provincial benefits paid in respect of a week have been taken into account for the purpose of section 76.4, no benefits paid under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act in respect of a week shall be taken into account for the same purpose.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.39 (src:1355)
GIVEN `provincial benefits paid in respect of a week have been taken into account for the purpose of section 76.4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.39 benefits paid under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act in respect of a week may be taken into account for that same purpose` IF
    NOT `provincial benefits paid in respect of a week have been taken into account for the purpose of section 76.4`

§ `Regulation 76.4 -- payment of benefits`

-- src:1358 | 76.4 (1) Subject to subsection (3), the provincial benefits paid to a self-employed person in respect of a week in a benefit period are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act if the self-employed person would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act, and any week in respect of which the self-employed person receives provincial benefits counts as a week for the purpose of calculating
-- src:1359 | (a) the overall maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together; and
-- src:1360 | (b) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(1) (src:1358-1360)
GIVEN `the self-employed person would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.4(1) the provincial benefits paid for the week are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act` IF
    `the self-employed person would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(1)(a) (src:1358-1359)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.4(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` MEANS
    `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` PLUS `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(1)(b) (src:1358, 1360)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.4(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act` MEANS
    `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` PLUS `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`

-- The weeks left within a maximum (out of range: Act s 152.14, piece ei5): the maximum less the weeks counted, as
-- reg 76.19(1)(a) and (b) do for Part III.1. More weeks counted than the maximum allows: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(1)(a) (src:1358-1359)
GIVEN `the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.4(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` MEANS
    IF `reg 76.4(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`
           AT MOST `the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together`
    THEN JUST (`the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together`
                   MINUS `reg 76.4(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(1)(b) (src:1358, 1360)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.4(1)(b) the weeks left within the maximum under subsection 152.14(2)` MEANS
    IF `reg 76.4(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`
           AT MOST `the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act`
    THEN JUST (`the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act`
                   MINUS `reg 76.4(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 152.14(2) of the Act` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1361 | (2) A benefit period is deemed to be established when a benefit period was established under a provincial law, and it is deemed to have begun the same week as the period established under the provincial law if the self-employed person would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(2) (src:1361)
GIVEN `a benefit period was established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.4(2) a benefit period is deemed to be established` IF
    `a benefit period was established under a provincial law`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(2) (src:1361)
GIVEN `a benefit period was established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first week of the period established under the provincial law` IS A DATE
      `the self-employed person would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 76.4(2) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` MEANS
    IF     `a benefit period was established under a provincial law`
       AND `the self-employed person would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period`
    THEN JUST `the first week of the period established under the provincial law`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) and (4): the accelerated-rate conversion and its rounding are reg 76.19(2) and (3) over again, so the rules call those.
-- src:1362 | (3) If the provincial benefits may be paid at an accelerated rate, such that the maximum amount of a particular type of provincial benefit may be paid to a self-employed person over fewer weeks, and the self-employed person is paid those benefits at the accelerated rate, the number of weeks of benefits that those weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act shall be determined by multiplying the number of weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the self-employed person by the result obtained by dividing the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate by the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(3) (src:1362)
GIVEN `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the self-employed person` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.4(3) the number of weeks of benefits that the weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act, before rounding` MEANS
    `reg 76.19(2) the number of weeks of benefits that the weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act, before rounding`
        `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the self-employed person`
        `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate`
        `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate`

-- src:1363 | (4) If the determination of the number of weeks under subsection (3) results in a number that contains a fraction of a week, the number shall be rounded to the nearest multiple of one week or, if the amount is equidistant from two multiples of one week, to the higher multiple.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(4) (src:1363)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.4(4) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` MEANS
    `reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` weeks

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(3) (src:1362)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.4(4) (src:1363)
GIVEN `the self-employed person is paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the self-employed person` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.4(3) and (4) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` MEANS
    `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act`
        `the self-employed person is paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate`
        `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the self-employed person`
        `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate`
        `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate`

§ `Regulation 76.41 -- weeks of provincial benefits beyond the maximum under the Act`

-- Same as reg 76.2, with the maxima of paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) or (b) and (2)(a) or (b) of the Act (inputs).
-- src:1364 | 76.41 If the maximum number of weeks referred to in paragraph 152.14(1)(a) or (b) or (2)(a) or (b) of the Act is less than the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid, the excess number of weeks for which provincial benefits may be paid shall not be taken into account for the purpose of determining the maximum number of weeks referred to in that paragraph.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.41 (src:1364)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks under the Act for the reason` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.41 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` MEANS
    `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks`
        `the maximum number of weeks under the Act for the reason`
        `the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid`
        `the weeks of provincial benefits paid`

§ `Regulation 76.42 -- persons making claims under different regimes`

-- src:1367 | 76.42 (1) Subsection (2) applies in respect of two persons who are caring for the same child or children and who do not reside in the same province at the time the first one of them makes an application under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act or an application for provincial benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.42(1) (src:1367)
GIVEN `two persons are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they do not reside in the same province at the time the first one of them makes an application under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act or an application for provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.42(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` IF
        `two persons are caring for the same child or children`
    AND `they do not reside in the same province at the time the first one of them makes an application under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act or an application for provincial benefits`

-- (2): the self-employed person's share, the arithmetic of reg 76.21(2).
-- src:1368 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), if one of the two persons referred to in subsection (1) has applied for and is entitled to receive benefits under section 152.05 of the Act (referred to in this section as “the self-employed person”) and the other person has applied for and is entitled to receive provincial benefits (referred to in this section as “the provincial applicant”), unless they have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks of such benefits they will each respectively apply for or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks of benefits,
-- src:1369 | (a) if the number of weeks of benefits that the self-employed person would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 152.05 of the Act is an even number, the number of weeks of benefits payable to the self-employed person is half that number; and
-- src:1370 | (b) if that number is an odd number,
-- src:1371 | (i) if the self-employed person made the earlier application, one week of those benefits plus half of the remaining weeks of benefits is payable to the self-employed person, and
-- src:1372 | (ii) if the provincial applicant made the earlier application, half the number of weeks of benefits remaining, after deducting one week, are payable to the self-employed person.
