§ `Regulation 76.421 -- waiving of the waiting period`

-- Paragraph 40(6)(b) (out of range: reg 40, piece er3), read as in reg 76.22.
-- src:1385 | 76.421 The reference in paragraph 40(6)(b) to “allowances, payments or other moneys are payable to the claimant by the claimant’s employer or former employer as sick leave pay” shall be read as a reference to “allowances, payments or other moneys were payable to the claimant by the claimant’s employer or former employer as sick leave pay or provincial benefits were paid to the claimant”.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.421 (src:1385)
GIVEN `allowances, payments or other moneys were payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provincial benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.421 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` IF
        `allowances, payments or other moneys were payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay`
    OR  `provincial benefits were paid to the claimant`

§ `Regulation 76.43 -- interprovincial mobility`

-- The self-employed person ceased to reside in a province with a plan and entered into an agreement under s 152.02 within
-- 12 months before the day they ceased to reside, or within three months after it. Then, if they were covered by that plan
-- during the 12 months before that day, they are deemed to satisfy the condition in paragraph 152.07(1)(a) (out of range:
-- piece ei5). Both ends of each window are included; month counts go through `add months`, which clamps.
-- src:1388 | 76.43 A self-employed person who has ceased to reside in a province that has a plan established under a provincial law and who entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act within 12 months before the day on which they ceased to reside in the province or within three months after that day is deemed, in order to qualify for the benefits payable under sections 152.04 and 152.05 of the Act, to have satisfied the condition set out in paragraph 152.07(1)(a) of the Act if they were covered by that plan during the 12 months before the day on which they ceased to reside in the province.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.43 (src:1388)
GIVEN `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law` IS A DATE
      `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.43 the agreement was entered into within 12 months before the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province, or within three months after that day` IF
        (    `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` AT MOST `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law`
         AND `add months` `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` 12 AT LEAST `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law`)
    OR  (    `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` GREATER THAN `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law`
         AND `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` AT MOST `add months` `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law` 3)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.43 (src:1388)
GIVEN `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law` IS A DATE
      `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the self-employed person was covered by that plan during the 12 months before the day they ceased to reside in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.43 the self-employed person is deemed to have satisfied the condition set out in paragraph 152.07(1)(a) of the Act` IF
        `reg 76.43 the agreement was entered into within 12 months before the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province, or within three months after that day`
            `the day the self-employed person ceased to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law`
            `the day the self-employed person entered into an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act`
    AND `the self-employed person was covered by that plan during the 12 months before the day they ceased to reside in the province`

§ `Regulations 76.44 and 76.45 -- administration`

-- src:1391 | 76.44 A self-employed person’s social insurance number shall be used for the purpose of facilitating the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained with respect to a self-employed person under provincial law or the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.44 (src:1391)
GIVEN `the use is for the purpose of facilitating the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained with respect to the self-employed person under provincial law or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.44 the self-employed person's social insurance number is to be used` IF
    `the use is for the purpose of facilitating the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained with respect to the self-employed person under provincial law or the Act`

-- src:1392 | 76.45 The Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose to a province that has a plan established under a provincial law information necessary for the administration of this Part that has been obtained by that Agency or that Minister under the Act or these Regulations and any information prepared from that information.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.45 (src:1392)
GIVEN `the province has a plan established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for the administration of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was obtained by that Agency or that Minister under the Act or these Regulations, or was prepared from information so obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.45 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` IF
        `the province has a plan established under a provincial law`
    AND `the information is necessary for the administration of this Part`
    AND `the information was obtained by that Agency or that Minister under the Act or these Regulations, or was prepared from information so obtained`
